For planet-moon system, the angular velocity of barycenter of planet-moon system is

$$
F _ {c e n t r i f u g a l - b a r y} = F _ {s t a r - b a r y}
$$

$$
(M _ {p} + M _ {m}) \omega_ {p} ^ {2} a _ {p} = \frac {G M _ {*} (M _ {p} + M _ {m})}{a _ {p} ^ {2}}
$$

$$
\omega_ {p} ^ {2} = \frac {G M _ {*}}{a _ {p} ^ {3}}
$$

For exomoon at Lagrange point $\mathbf{L}_1$ or $\mathbf{L}_2$ ,

$$
F _ {\text {c e n t r i f u g a l - m o o n}} = F _ {\text {s t a r - m o o n}} \pm F _ {\text {p l a n e t - m o o n}}
$$

$$
M _ {m} W _ {p} ^ {2} \left(a _ {p} \pm a _ {m}\right) = \frac {G M _ {*} M _ {m}}{\left(a _ {p} \pm a _ {m}\right) ^ {2}} \pm \frac {G M _ {p} M _ {m}}{\left(a _ {p b} + a _ {m}\right) ^ {2}}
$$

$$
\frac {M _ {*} \left(a _ {p} \pm a _ {m}\right)}{a _ {p} ^ {3}} = \frac {M _ {*}}{\left(a _ {p} \pm a _ {m}\right) ^ {2}} \pm \frac {M _ {p}}{\left(a _ {p b} + a _ {m}\right) ^ {2}}
$$

Since $M_p >> M_m$ and $a_{pb} << a_m$

$$
\frac {M _ {*} \left(a _ {p} \pm a _ {m}\right)}{a _ {p} ^ {3}} = \frac {M _ {*}}{\left(a _ {p} \pm a _ {m}\right) ^ {2}} \pm \frac {M _ {p}}{a _ {m} ^ {2}}
$$

$$
M _ {*} \left(a _ {p} \pm a _ {m}\right) ^ {3} a _ {m} ^ {2} = M _ {*} a _ {p} ^ {3} a _ {m} ^ {2} \pm M _ {p} a _ {p} ^ {3} \left(a _ {p} \pm a _ {m}\right) ^ {2}
$$

$$
M _ {*} \left(\pm 3 a _ {p} ^ {2} a _ {m} ^ {3} + 3 a _ {p} a _ {m} ^ {4} \pm a _ {m} ^ {5}\right) = \pm M _ {p} a _ {p} ^ {3} \left(a _ {p} \pm a _ {m}\right) ^ {2}
$$

For $a _ {p} \gg a _ {m}$, $M _ {*} \left(3 a _ {p} ^ {2} a _ {m} ^ {3}\right) \gg M _ {p} a _ {p} ^ {5}$

$$
a _ {m} ^ {3} = \frac {M _ {p}}{3 M _ {*}} a _ {p} ^ {3}
$$

$$
a _ {m} = a _ {p} \sqrt [ 3 ]{\frac {M _ {p}}{3 M _ {*}}}
$$

Thus $x = 3$.

The radius of the Hill sphere of this planetary system is

$$
R _ {h} = a _ {p} \sqrt [ 3 ]{\frac {M _ {p}}{3 M _ {*}}}
$$

$$
R _ {h} = 6.75 \times 10 ^ {9} \times \sqrt [ 3 ]{\frac {120 \times 5.98 \times 10 ^ {24}}{3 \times 1.99 \times 10 ^ {30}}} \mathrm{m}
$$

$$
R _ {h} = 3.33 \times 10 ^ {8} \mathrm{m} = 52.2 R _ {\oplus}
$$

\boxed{x = 3}, \boxed{R_{h} = 52.2 R_{\oplus}}

From Roche limit equation

$$
R _ {r} = 1.26 R _ {p} \sqrt [ 3 ]{\frac {\rho_ {p}}{\rho_ {m}}}
$$

$$
R _ {r} = 1.26 \times 12 \times \sqrt [ 3 ]{\frac {120 / (12) ^ {3}}{1}} R _ {\oplus}
$$

$$
R _ {r} = 6.21 R _ {\oplus}
$$

\boxed{R_{r} = 6.21 R_{\oplus}}

